  "implementation": [
    "RHS values are evaluated once against the real pre-BEFORE row. Rowid conversion precedes ordinary columns; ordinary SET expressions follow physical column order. The candidate applies affinity and computes generated registers before BEFORE/type checks. Effective values are reified as compiler-private bound expressions, retaining real subtypes and every original syntactic SET name.",
    "Register demand is derived from actual trigger WHEN/body ASTs with the ordinary read compiler supplying real source schemas. Scope traversal distinguishes local aliases from trigger parameters and handles captured/derived SELECTs. It reproduces the pinned 32-bit NEW mask behavior, including high-column saturation and unconditional loads above column 31. Unrequested ordinary registers start NULL before generated calculation, as in SQLite; actual writes reload all unassigned physical columns and recompute generated values.",
    "Actual value and subtype registers are captured by the ordinary RETURNING evaluator before AFTER programs. A transient compiler-only projection context permits generated capture fields; the original user RETURNING is validated first with the ordinary source limit. The private flag is restored before trigger execution, with a registered kernel theorem. Wide-table capture and invalid 2001-column source controls compare against SQLite.",
    "Trigger Param frames require OLD/NEW qualification and carry no column comparison affinity, while retaining real collation, value representation and subtype. Current local table names win. At the next lexical scope, trigger parameters precede correlated outer aliases. Ordinary correlated frames retain their original affinity and visibility behavior.",
    "NOT NULL, IGNORE/REPLACE, CHECK repair, STRICT timing, generated values, datatype/error order, skipped deleted/rekeyed rows and immediate FK counter behavior are independently exercised. BEFORE/AFTER register metadata stays transient and does not alter persistent SQLite records."
  ],
  "reference_protocol": "Complete stdout/exit/first-error and independently observed persisted catalog/table/integrity contents compare against pinned SQLite 3.53.4 in both public file modes. Twelve generated BEFORE inputs are regenerated for the fresh final checkpoint. Alias, high-column, 1025-column table, source-limit, private-function, FK and negative-constraint controls remain real failures until fixed; no skip or oracle correction is used.",
  "crash_scope": "SIGKILL timing samples for BEFORE UPDATE writes to two tables, fixed OLD/NEW body values and frozen SET values overriding an intermediate body mutation of a uniquely indexed target. Public Lean recovery followed by independent SQLite catalog/root-zero/rowid/schema-cookie/row/integrity checks. Complete old or new states are required. No every-syscall, power-loss or arbitrary-schedule claim.",
  "primary_source_basis": "Pinned update.c regNew population, NEW column mask, pre-BEFORE affinity, surviving-row seek, unmodified-column reload and generated recomputation; insert.c STRICT table affinity; expr.c/resolve.c trigger parameter affinity and lexical lookup; native subtype/limit behavior. Outcomes are independently checked by the pinned reference.",
  "proof_scope": "Retained Core/file/physical and signed-counter contracts compile. New audited component laws cover a zero-subtype register reification and successful point execution restoring its caller projection context. New executable group checks provisional generated NULLs, actual after-reload values and real BEFORE/AFTER JSON subtype registers. No complete UPDATE/VDBE equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "BEFORE INSERT, INSTEAD OF/temp triggers, RAISE, recursive_triggers settings, triggered UPSERT, trigger-aware ALTER, wider query/constraint/error and FK combinations remain work. Supported trigger timing is still an admitted slice.",
    "Eight of 88 named probes still fail: WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys and partial/expression indexes, both modes. These probes do not define global coverage.",
    "UTF-16 writes/setters, native-key/materialization limits, pending new physical allocations and earlier SQL/storage limitations remain. The finite process-kill samples do not establish every syscall/power-loss schedule."
  ],
